    {
      "text": "many bodies of the saints which slept arose, Matt. 27:52 (Hel. 14:25; 3 Ne. 23:9–11). heard … evil he hath done to thy saints, Acts 9:13. to the saints which dwelt at Lydda, Acts 9:32. when he had called the saints and widows, Acts 9:41. beloved of God, called to be saints, Rom. 1:7. he maketh intercession for the saints, Rom. 8:27. Distributing to the necessity of saints, Rom. 12:13. I go unto Jerusalem to minister unto the saints, Rom. 15:25. sanctified in Christ Jesus, called to be saints, 1 Cor. 1:2. saints shall judge the world, 1 Cor. 6:2. author … of peace, as in all churches of the saints, 1 Cor. 14:33. saints which are in all Achaia, 2 Cor. 1:1. fellowship of the ministering to the saints, 2 Cor. 8:4. not only supplieth the want of the saints, 2 Cor. 9:12. to the saints which are at Ephesus, Eph. 1:1. no more strangers … but fellowcitizens with the saints, Eph. 2:19. who am less than the least of all saints, Eph. 3:8. For the perfecting of the saints, Eph. 4:12 (D&C 124:143). fornication … let it not be once named among you, as becometh saints, Eph. 5:3. all perseverance and supplication for all saints, Eph. 6:18. saints in Christ Jesus which are at Philippi, Philip. 1:1. To the saints and faithful brethren, Col. 1:2. coming of our Lord … with all his saints, 1 Thes. 3:13. he shall come to be glorified in his saints, 2 Thes. 1:10. ye have ministered to the saints, Heb. 6:10. Salute … all the saints, Heb. 13:24. contend for the faith which was once delivered unto the saints, Jude 1:3. odours, which are the prayers of saints, Rev. 5:8. offer it with the prayers of all saints, Rev. 8:3. the patience and the faith of the saints, Rev. 13:10 (14:12). thou King of saints, Rev. 15:3. they have shed the blood of saints, Rev. 16:6. woman drunken with the blood of the saints, Rev. 17:6. in her was found the blood of prophets, and of saints, Rev. 18:24. they … compassed the camp of the saints about, Rev. 20:9.",
